# The kbootset each row of the major registry needs (C2-2 section 1.2,
# version 7): the oldest kbootset package version whose registry has the
# row and writes it into a module kernel's major table (core patch 0051).
# One line per row of `majors`, in its order: c (character) or b (block),
# the major, the version; `-` until a published kbootset carries the row.
# Rows of 1.1 give 1.1.0.261101-34, the first kbootset to write the table.
# A module package's kbootset floor (its pkginfo APKG_KBOOTSET=, or a
# kbootset.conf line) is at least the version here of each major it owns;
# gen-catalog refuses a module package whose floor is lower.
c 48 1.1.0.261101-34
c 49 1.1.0.261101-34
c 51 1.1.0.261101-34
c 52 1.1.0.261101-34
c 53 1.1.0.261101-34
c 54 1.1.0.261101-34
c 55 1.1.0.261101-34
c 56 1.1.0.261114-45
c 68 1.1.0.261115-46
b 20 1.1.0.261101-34
